msgid "Apache Camel on Quarkus"
msgstr "Apache Camel on Quarkus"

msgid ""
"https://camel.apache.org/[Apache Camel] is the Swiss knife of integrating "
"heterogeneous systems with more than a decade of history and a lively "
"community of users and developers. It offers 350+ connectors covering "
"various protocols, file formats, messaging systems, databases, APIs and "
"cloud services, so you can integrate almost anything without writing custom "
"adapter code."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Camel Quarkus turns Camel components into Quarkus extensions, so routes are "
"wired at build time and live-reloaded in dev mode."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The https://camel.apache.org/camel-quarkus/[Apache Camel Quarkus "
"documentation] covers getting started, the list of supported extensions, "
"configuration, observability, testing and native mode."
msgstr ""

msgid "Defining a route"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Generate a project with the `camel-quarkus-kafka`, `camel-quarkus-jackson` "
"and `camel-quarkus-direct` extensions from https://code.quarkus.io/?e=org."
"apache.camel.quarkus:camel-quarkus-kafka&e=org.apache.camel.quarkus:camel-"
"quarkus-jackson&e=org.apache.camel.quarkus:camel-quarkus-direct[code.quarkus."
"io], then declare the route as a CDI bean:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A route is a processing pipeline: it consumes messages from an endpoint "
"(`direct:order-placed`), transforms them, and sends them to one or more "
"endpoints (`kafka:order-events`).\n"
"A `ProducerTemplate` is available as a CDI bean, so existing code, such as a "
"JAX-RS resource, can feed the route with `producerTemplate.sendBody(\"direct:"
"order-placed\", order)`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Run `./mvnw quarkus:dev`: Dev Services starts a Kafka broker and the route "
"publishes each order as JSON to the `order-events` topic.\n"
"Camel routes are hot-reloaded, so changes take effect on save."
msgstr ""

